Third-party components
----------------------

Linked libraries (AGPL-3.0-only):
  - libsignal              https://github.com/signalapp/libsignal
  - libsignal-service-rs   https://github.com/whisperfish/libsignal-service-rs
  - presage                https://github.com/whisperfish/presage
  - RingRTC (calls)        https://github.com/signalapp/ringrtc

Calls use WebRTC (BSD-3-Clause), Copyright (c) 2011, The WebRTC project
authors, linked from Signal's prebuilt library through RingRTC. Its license
and the licenses of the libraries it includes ship with that library, in
LICENSE.md next to libwebrtc.a (target/webrtc/release after a build).
Camera capture uses nokhwa (Apache-2.0).

Bundled data and assets:
  - Emoji data from emojibase-data 17.0.0 (MIT), Copyright (c) 2017-2019
    Miles Johnson. See crates/emoji/data/LICENSE-emojibase.
  - Icons from Lucide (ISC), Copyright (c) Lucide Icons and Contributors,
    bundled through gpui-kit.
  - Message status and error icons from Signal Desktop (AGPL-3.0-only),
    Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC. See crates/app/assets/icons/signal.
  - The ringtone from Signal Desktop (sounds/ringtone_minimal.ogg,
    AGPL-3.0-only), Copyright Signal Messenger, LLC, converted to AAC. See
    crates/app/assets/sounds.

JPEG optimization uses mozjpeg (IJG, BSD-3-Clause and Zlib licenses):
  This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

Other Rust dependencies (gpui, gpui-kit, oxipng, linkify, fst, sqlx and
others) are under MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD or similar permissive licenses. To
list every dependency with its license text, run `cargo about generate` or
`cargo deny list` and include the result with any binary you distribute.
